Bridge 0124: shrink a render pass's render area to the bounds of what its draws may write (their Vulkan scissors,
already clipped to their viewports; clear_reach::DrawnArea), aligned outward to 32 px and clamped to the target.
CoreAnimation's full-size passes often draw only inside a dirty rect, yet Turnip loaded and stored the whole target in
GMEM; its load/store blits are scissored to the render area (tu6_emit_blit_scissor), so this saves that traffic.
Kept whole: executions, pending pipelines, tile dispatches, imageblocks, any resolve, samples > 1, sample planes, a Clear
load of a non-memoryless attachment, unbounded or no draws. Logs `SWEET_M2V_RENDER_AREA RA shrunk N passes ...`.
Knob: SWEET_M2V_RENDER_AREA (off unless set and not 0; off = same results and same work as before).

